ich is the main content of this fragment), skip sensors that only appear in changelog prose. Actually, revision 2 says \"Addition of the CMF010, CMF025 and CMF050 sensors\" — meaning these sensors ARE part of the certified types. And CMFHC too. Including them doesn't fabricate. I'll include a components entry for measurement sensors with those designations.\n\nHmm, but the fragment-only instruction... The changelog tells us these are certified components. I'll include. Let me finalize components:\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"role\": \"measurement sensor\", \"type_designations\": [\"CMF010\", \"CMF025\", \"CMF050\", \"CMFHC\"]},\n  {\"role\": \"transmitter electronics\", \"type_designations\": [\"5700\"]},\n  {\"role\": \"core processor\", \"type_designations\": [\"MVD800 Enhanced Core Processor\", \"5700 internal core processor\"], \"alternatives\": \"OR\"}\n]\n```\n\nNow footnotes array:\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"marker\": \"*)\", \"text\": \"The transmitter software and the Weights & Measures (W&M) software form a matched set. Please note that the W&M software does not have a checksum and means W&M is licensed.\"},\n  {\"marker\": \"*)\", ...}\n]\n```\n\nWait, note is \"*)\" and \"**)\" per the markdown. Keep markers as \"*)\" and \"**)\". But in the table they appear as `<sup>*)</sup>` — same.\n\n- marker: \"*\", text: \"The transmitter software and the Weights & Measures (W&M) software form a matched set. Please note that the W&M software does not have a checksum and means W&M is licensed.\"\n- marker: \"**\", text: \"The number between brackets, is the transmitter software which belongs to the stated checksum.\"\n\nNow matrix_tables details. Also there's \"Table 7\" title: \"Software versions of the 5700 electronics\". Name it that.\n\nLet me also decide whether the environmental table needs a matrix_tables entry — no, it fits characteristics.\n\nFull JSON:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"certificate\": {\n    \"number\": \"R117/2007-A-NL1-21.02\",\n    \"scheme\": \"A\",\n    \"project_n